<title>UK: Lloyds Abbey Life says no comment on rumours.</title>
<headline>Lloyds Abbey Life says no comment on rumours.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British life insurer Lloyds Abbey Life Plc said on Wednesday it did not comment on market rumours after speculation about its future ownership sent its share price sharply higher.</p>
<p>Its shares were trading at 593 pence, up 32.5 pence, just off the days highs at 607 pence.</p>
<p>&quot;The company doesn't comment on market rumours,&quot; an official said.</p>
<p>The market had been swirling with rumours that giant insurer Prudential Corp wanted to buy the insurance group, which is 62 percent owned by Lloyds TSB Group Plc.  </p>
<p>Analysts suggested a more likely scenario was that the Lloyds TSB banking group wanted to increase its stake in the insurer.</p>
<p>Prudential and Lloyds TSB both said they did not comment on market rumours.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5113</p>
